.el .ds Aq '
.TH MERMAN-CLI-LINT 1 2026-08-15 "Merman 0.8.0-alpha.6" "Merman CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
merman\-cli\-lint \- Analyze Mermaid source and print diagnostics JSON or text
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmerman\-cli lint\fR [\fB\-\-stdin\-file\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-pretty\fR] [\fB\-\-markdown\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-runtime\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-clock\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-timezone\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-random\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-timing\fR] [\fB\-\-fixed\-today\fR] [\fB\-\-fixed\-local\-offset\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-\-lint\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-enable\-rule\fR] [\fB\-\-disable\-rule\fR] [\fB\-\-rule\-severity\fR] [\fB\-\-resource\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-resource\-limit\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIINPUT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Analyze Mermaid source and print diagnostics JSON or text
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-pretty\fR
Pretty\-print JSON output
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIINPUT\fR]
Input Mermaid or Markdown file. Use `\-` for stdin
.SH "INPUT HANDLING"
.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\-file\-name\fR \fI<STDIN_FILE_NAME>\fR
Optional file name to use when linting stdin
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format for diagnostics
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
text
.RE
.SH "ANALYSIS OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-markdown\fR
Include Markdown fence diagnostics by scanning `.md`, `.markdown`, or `.mdx` input
.SH "MERMAID CONFIGURATION"
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\-file\fR \fI<CONFIG_FILE>\fR
JSON Mermaid configuration file
.SH "RUNTIME POLICY"
.TP
\fB\-\-runtime\fR \fI<POLICY>\fR [default: deterministic]
Runtime source for clock, local timezone, and operation randomness
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
deterministic
.IP \(bu 2
native
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-clock\fR
Use the system clock while keeping other runtime sources deterministic
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-timezone\fR
Use the system local timezone while keeping other runtime sources deterministic
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-random\fR
Use system randomness while keeping other runtime sources deterministic
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-timing\fR
Enable operation timing diagnostics through the compiled system timing adapter
.TP
\fB\-\-fixed\-today\fR \fI<FIXED_TODAY>\fR
Override the local "today" date for time\-dependent diagrams
.TP
\fB\-\-fixed\-local\-offset\-minutes\fR \fI<FIXED_LOCAL_OFFSET_MINUTES>\fR
Override the local timezone offset in minutes for time\-dependent diagrams
.SH "LINT RULES"
.TP
\fB\-\-lint\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Built\-in lint rule profile: core, recommended, or strict
.TP
\fB\-\-enable\-rule\fR \fI<RULE_ID>\fR
Enable a configurable lint rule by stable rule id. Can be repeated
.TP
\fB\-\-disable\-rule\fR \fI<RULE_ID>\fR
Disable a configurable lint rule by stable rule id. Can be repeated
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\-severity\fR \fI<RULE_ID=SEVERITY>\fR
Override a configurable lint rule severity as RULE_ID=error|warning|info|hint. Can be repeated
.SH "RESOURCE CONTROLS"
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR [default: trusted\-native]
Resource policy for input, semantic models, output, and CLI acquisition.

Use interactive for cooperative editor\-like workloads, constrained for untrusted or multi\-tenant input, and trusted\-native for controlled local workloads. The unbounded profile retains hard implementation and protocol guards.
.sp
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
interactive: General interactive applications and public binding surfaces
.IP \(bu 2
constrained: Constrained rendering for untrusted or publicly submitted documents
.IP \(bu 2
trusted\-native: Local CLI and controlled native batch rendering
.IP \(bu 2
unbounded\-for\-trusted\-input: Explicitly disable policy budgets while retaining hard backend capabilities
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-resource\-limit\fR \fI<STABLE_ID=POSITIVE_U64>\fR
Override a resource budget as STABLE_ID=POSITIVE_U64. Can be repeated
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  merman\-cli lint diagram.mmd
  merman\-cli lint \-\-format json diagram.mmd

More options: `merman\-cli lint \-\-help` shows advanced rule, runtime, and resource controls.
.SH VERSION
v0.8.0\-alpha.6
